 fear and violence  diplomacy although that also begs the  question of whether or not the  federation holds samus accountable for  the destruction of the research station  which had all of their metroid research  and whatever else they had going on  inside in the events of metroid fusion  if you'll recall samus clearly acts  against the federation's orders when she  you know sends the research station into  the planet sr-388 and blows them both to  kingdom come but again since there has  been no blowback that we know of from  the federation by the events of metroid  5 it can be assumed that samus was able  to convince the federation of her  reasons for disobedience and now all is  well and good and peachy between the two  parties so really there aren't any  unanswered loose ends as far as the 2d  metroid games before dread are concerned  there is however a glaring loose end  that happens at the current end of the  metroid prime series though which takes  place in its entirety between the 2d  games metroid 1 and 2. for those in the  know you'll recall that at the end of  metroid prime 3 corruption samus is  shown being followed by the mysterious  bounty hunter psylux into deep space the  story then continues in metroid prime  federation force which everyone bought  and played when at the end of that game  we're shown a pov perspective of psylux  as the mystery dude stumbles upon an  infant metroid obviously this has huge  implications but as far as whether it  will affect the story of metroid 6 i  personally find it unlikely since we  have metroid prime 4 in the works  allegedly i'm about 50 convinced we all  hallucinated it but should metroid prime  4 ever actually release we can only  assume that it would take place after  metroid prime federation force anyway my  point with all of this is that no matter  what we look at at which point in the  series everything that could be a  potential storyline in the franchise  leading up to metroid dread is either  explainable or has another outlet coming  that we know isn't going to be metroid  6. so that leaves us with only one  option is there anything left unanswered  in metroid dread itself that could lead  to another game based off of dread well  my friends i am here to tell you that  absolutely yes there is recall with me  if you will the events of the end of the  game samus has to travel to the second  to final area on the surface of zdr  called hanubia where her ship is only  adam tells her that she can't leave just  yet she's got to face ravenbeak because  if she doesn't kill him or at least try  to kill him he's just gonna escape and  do the same thing somewhere else right  as you traverse around the area you even  see some clearly active ships hovering  in the distance so you're thinking to  yourself okay yeah i see that he might  escape so samus does exactly what adam  said to do and finds this extremely cool  thrown seat and flying sphere thing and  travels upwards above the surface of  ziti are two raven beaks levitating  fortress called iturash and it is here  that ravenbeek reveals that he was adam  the whole time and that samus is  essentially his dna shared daughter and  then has the life sucked out of him by  his aforementioned daughter not only  does daddy's girl suck the life force  metroid style out of her old man she  also does this to the entire flying  fortress of aitorash crashing the whole  system into hanubia on the surface of  zdr but alas ravenbeak was hurt but not  killed and after both he and his little  girl get up and see that each other is  still alive an ex-parasite takes control  of ravenbeak's body turning him into  crane actually but then getting killed  for good by metroid samus and then the  planet starts to blow up for some reason  probably because of iturosh crashing  into the planet like the space research  lab in metroid fusion anyway metroid  samus has to book it out of there but  here at the very end of the game is  where the biggest loose 