e chozo ships could move from  the background is if they were flown  away by the ex-possessed chozo warriors  you know this was a deliberate detail  put in the game that in my opinion was  meant to tease samus's next adventure  which we can only assume will be metroid  6. and like i said now that the x  parasite not only has survived yet  another destruction attempt but also has  wings with which to fly anywhere they  want to in the galaxy there's no telling  how fast how far or how badly the x will  spread but one thing's per certain they  literally have limitless potential like  never before meaning there could be an  infinite number of x parasites by the  time the next game takes place and with  their only predator the metroid's being  completely extinct except for samus  aaron the last metroid in existence well  it seems to me that the ultimate  showdown between the metroid species and  the infinite x parasite has yet to  happen and who knows maybe it will end  with the destruction of both parasitic  species once and for all but this is all  just my theory what do you guys think  could it be that the ex-parasite was  responsible for flying the mysterious  chozo ships away at the end of metroid  dread or did a game developer just  forget to put him back in there at the  end of the game let me know in the  comments below also thank you so much  for watching please consider liking this  video if you liked the video to get  metroid spread around on youtube because  samus deserves it and subscribe to the  channel for so many more interesting  gaming videos to come that will knock  your socks off huge thanks as always to  my fantastic bandit crew who make my day  every day that's all i've got for this  one so as always i hope you have a  wonderful rest of your day this is mask  nintendo abandoned looking forward to  seeing you next time and signing out  [Music]  you

